<title>COLOMBIA: Banco de Colombia net profits down.</title>
<headline>Banco de Colombia net profits down.</headline>
<dateline>BOGOTA 1997-02-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>Banco de Colombia, Colombia's second largest bank in terms of assets, reported the following 1996 results in a report Thursday:</p>
<p>Net profits 51.17 billion pesos vs 54.4 billion in 1995</p>
<p>Total assets 3.1 trillion pesos, up 30.4 percent from 1995</p>
<p>Proposed share dividend 14 pesos vs 20 pesos in 1995. Note: These are unconsolidated figures and are subject to revison by the banking superintendency.</p>
<p>((--Juan Guillermo Londono, Bogota newsroom, 571 610 7944))</p>
</text>
